Sidejacking with Wireshark (Single Kali Machine)
Quick Start
bash
# Start services
sudo systemctl start apache2 mysql

# Open DVWA
firefox http://localhost/dvwa
Step 1: Login to DVWA
Go to: http://localhost/dvwa

Login: admin / password

Set Security Level to Low

Step 2: Capture Cookie with Wireshark
bash
# Open Wireshark
sudo wireshark
In Wireshark:
Select interface: lo (loopback)

Start capture

Filter: http and ip.addr == 127.0.0.1

Refresh DVWA page in browser

Look for Cookie: in packets

Copy PHPSESSID value (e.g., abc123def456)

Step 3: Hijack the Session
Option A: Browser Method
Open new private window: firefox --private-window http://localhost/dvwa

Press F12 → Storage tab → Cookies

Add cookie:

Name: PHPSESSID

Value: [your-copied-value]

Domain: localhost

Refresh page

Option B: Command Line
bash
curl -b "PHPSESSID=abc123def456" http://localhost/dvwa/
Step 4: Verify Success
You should see "Welcome to Damn Vulnerable Web App!" without logging in

Shows "Logged in as 'admin'"

Troubleshooting
bash
# No packets? Check services
sudo systemctl status apache2
sudo systemctl status mysql

# Test DVWA access
curl -I http://localhost/dvwa/
Security Fixes
Use HTTPS instead of HTTP

Set cookies with: HttpOnly;Secure;SameSite=Strict

Short session timeouts

Clean Up
bash
sudo systemctl stop apache2 mysql